WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.480
Hello.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.120
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.760
In this ninth lesson, we'll look at the daily
habits that help you overcome a mood disorder,

4
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.370
and the circadian rhythm behind them.

5
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:26.260
A rhythm that changes over a cycle of
one day is called a circadian rhythm.

6
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.500
The sleep-wake cycle and changes
in body temperature are examples.

7
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.500
Melatonin, which regulates sleep,
falls when light is bright.

8
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.840
People with a mood disorder are more sensitive to light,

9
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:44.640
so even one or two late nights on a
smartphone can quickly shift the rhythm.

10
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.420
When irregular meals and sleep pile
up and the rhythm breaks down,

11
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.600
you become less able to handle stress
and your mood swings grow wider.

12
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.690
Symptoms can then appear or get worse.

13
00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.290
Half of treating a mood disorder is
taking your medication steadily.

14
00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:09.020
The other half is a regular lifestyle,
exercise, and stress management.

15
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.580
Neither half alone can cure the illness.

16
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.190
Once a month, check yourself with
the Healthy Lifestyle Checklist.

17
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:22.270
If you keep a score of 80 or more,
the illness gradually improves,

18
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.600
and your risk of relapse can go down.

19
00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:31.440
It is best for the body to be
active by day and asleep at night.

20
00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.100
When you are depressed, you go to bed
later and later to soothe your mood,

21
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.900
sleep in the next morning, and feel even more depressed.

22
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.820
It's easy to fall into this vicious cycle.

23
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.060
Sleeping less may seem to lift your mood the next day.

24
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:52.480
But the depression comes back longer,
and your mood swings get worse.

25
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:57.750
First, get rid of the time you spend lying in bed awake.

26
00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:03.720
Watching TV or your smartphone in bed
makes it harder to fall asleep at night.

27
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:10.940
Second, get up at the same time every day,
even on days off and when you're tired.

28
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.700
If you get up late, you can't help going to bed late.

29
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.360
Third, avoid naps.

30
00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:23.080
If you are very sleepy, set an alarm
and sleep no more than 20 minutes.

31
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.840
Fourth, remove clocks and electronic
devices from the bedroom,

32
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.940
and keep your smartphone out of reach.

33
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.600
Fifth, let go of worrying about sleep.

34
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:41.470
Even if it's short, make time to fall
asleep naturally, and extend it gradually.

35
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:48.990
Sixth, make the room quiet and dark, and avoid
caffeine, and smoking and drinking before bed.

36
00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:52.350
Getting sunlight as soon as you wake up is good.

37
00:02:53.320 --> 00:03:00.950
Alcohol weakens the brain's mood-regulating circuit,
making an unstable mood even more unstable.

38
00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:07.350
While you are drunk, depression and anxiety
seem better and sleep seems to come.

39
00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.880
But as the alcohol wears off, you feel more
depressed and anxious, and you wake from sleep.

40
00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:20.780
Alcohol is also harmful to the liver and
interferes with how medication is broken down.

41
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.540
That is why quitting drinking is best for treatment.

42
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:30.060
If quitting is hard, drink as
little as possible, and not often.

43
00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.110
If one drink leads to another for
you, you need to quit completely.

44
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.280
Exercise by itself prevents depression and relapse.

45
00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:45.320
Seeing sunlight while you
exercise is especially effective.

46
00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:53.100
Even if you feel too low to do anything, go
outside every morning at 10 o'clock, even briefly,

47
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.020
and see the sunlight.

48
00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:00.886
When you feel a little better, take a
30-minute walk with family or a pet dog.

49
00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:05.536
When you feel better still, return
to the exercise you used to enjoy,

50
00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:07.840
or try walking 10,000 steps a day.

51
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.810
Exercising and talking with people
you're close to can work even better.

52
00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.080
Eating regularly is good too.

53
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.320
Have breakfast, and eat the same amount at set times.

54
00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:24.610
Dieting by skipping meals can make mood symptoms worse.

55
00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:30.450
When you're depressed, you crave carbohydrates
before bed, such as snacks, bread,

56
00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.190
or instant noodles.

57
00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:37.590
They seem to help while you eat, but you
end up more depressed and gain weight.

58
00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.130
For weight control, start with
small habits rather than big goals.

59
00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:47.510
Skip snacks, fill up on vegetables before
meals, avoid sweet foods and drinks,

60
00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.360
and write down what you eat.

61
00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:55.780
Binge eating is a symptom of the illness
and needs treatment, but habits matter too.

62
00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.710
During depressed periods, don't stock your home
with unhealthy foods that are easy to eat.

63
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.060
To escape depression quickly,

64
00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:11.680
it's easy to reach for things that change your
mood fast: drinking, gambling, overspending,

65
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:20.320
overambitious plans or investments, binge eating,
self-harm, substance misuse, or sleeping less.

66
00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.840
These seem to lift your mood for a moment,

67
00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.890
but in the end they bring you
back to the same depressed place.

68
00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:33.310
In contrast, a regular routine, walking
and exercise, yoga and meditation,

69
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.110
conversation and reading,

70
00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:40.390
and realistic plans that don't overreach
keep your mood steady for a long time,

71
00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.050
even though they take time.

72
00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:50.620
Go to sleep and wake up at the same time, stay
away from alcohol, get morning sunlight and walk,

73
00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.040
and eat regular meals.

74
00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:56.020
Small habits protect the rhythm of your mood.

75
00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:01.460
Next time, we'll look at the various
symptoms that can come with a mood disorder,

76
00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.300
and how to cope with them.

77
00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.400
Thank you.
